From 4614261075627c81c9bd146e44002dbf1d97cf11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slopdealer <326519127+slopdealer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:22:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 47/49] Many directories: restore hands work between its
 goroutines per batch, not per directory

Both passes of restore passed every directory through another goroutine and
back. In the first pass the node lookahead ends a batch at every directory,
so a run of directories came back one node per request, and an empty tree
cost a request and a reply for nothing. In the second pass the tree
prefetch handed over one prepared tree at a time through a queue of one.
Each hand-over puts one goroutine to sleep and wakes another, and every
wake-up sets idle CPUs searching for work: on a tree of 606,060 directories
that was 1.3 million voluntary context switches against 0.09 million in
stock, and user CPU that grew with the number of CPUs (19.8 s on 4 cores,
24.1 s on 16; stock 17.9 s on both).

First pass: nodes are decoded by the traversal itself until one is not a
directory; from that node on the helper prepares the following nodes ahead,
as before, until a directory ends the run. Second pass: the prepared trees
are handed over in batches of up to 64 trees and 256 KiB of prepared nodes.
A batch is handed over as soon as the traversal has room for it, so a
traversal that waits is still served tree by tree; only a traversal that is
busy lets the batch grow. Order, errors, the fallback to loading a tree
directly and the byte budget of a prepared tree are unchanged.

Measured (606,060 directories and three files, tmpfs, whole cores, wall /
user / voluntary context switches): 4 cores 25.8 s / 16.5 s / 0.09M (before
28.7 / 19.9 / 1.30M, stock 34.4 / 17.8 / 0.09M); 8 cores 26.7 / 18.4 /
0.11M (before 30.5 / 22.5 / 1.32M, stock 35.0 / 18.4); 16 cores 27.4 / 19.1
/ 0.11M (before 31.6 / 23.6 / 1.28M, stock 35.6 / 18.2).

Tests: TestNodeLookaheadDecodesDirectoryRunsInline (fails before),
TestNodeLookaheadRandomTreesKeepOrder, TestTreePrefetchHandsOverBatches,
TestTreePrefetchBatchKeepsByteBudget,
TestTreePrefetchDoesNotDelayAWaitingTraversal.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
